1. What you may do
You may use the Action free of charge in GitHub Actions workflows for repositories you own or are allowed to work on, including private and commercial repositories. GitHub may copy the Action onto its runners to run it. You may fork the repository on GitHub, as GitHub's terms allow, only to use the Action in your own workflows.

2. What you may not do
You may not:
- reverse engineer, decompile or deobfuscate the Action, or try to rebuild its source code, except where applicable law allows it despite this term;
